      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update trivy-fips to 0.69.3-r6 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-35206: a crafted Chart.yaml name containing a dot segment makes Helm write an extracted chart into the output directory itself instead of a subdirectory named after the chart, so it can overwrite files there; helm.sh/helm/v3 is fixed in 3.20.2 (https://github.com/helm/helm/security/advisories/GHSA-hr2v-4r36-88hr, https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5435). The Go build information of /usr/bin/trivy in each of the 37 published trivy-fips builds for Alpine 3.23 (0.69.1-r0 to 0.74.0-r11), on both x86_64 and aarch64, was read for this decision. Builds before 0.69.3-r6 embed helm.sh/helm/v3 3.19.2, which the advisory lists as affected. Builds from 0.69.3-r6 on embed helm.sh/helm/v3 3.20.2 (in some of them), which the advisory does not list as affected."
    },
